WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.540
Hello everybody, my name is Markiplier and welcome to That Dragon, Cancer.

00:00:03.540 --> 00:00:04.880
Now,
[sounds of nature in the background]

00:00:04.880 --> 00:00:07.120
you guys have wanted me to play this for a long time.

00:00:07.120 --> 00:00:08.840
And I've wanted to play it too.

00:00:08.840 --> 00:00:11.120
Ah, it's just that I have a very...

00:00:11.580 --> 00:00:14.820
I have a very close relationship with the topic of this game,

00:00:14.820 --> 00:00:16.260
and that is obviously cancer.

00:00:16.260 --> 00:00:18.960
Not me personally, um, but my dad, ah,

00:00:18.960 --> 00:00:22.300
had cancer when I was about 18 years old, and he died from it.

00:00:22.300 --> 00:00:25.120
And I'm not saying that's put me off from playing it, that's not what I'm

00:00:25.120 --> 00:00:27.900
saying at all. I'm not afraid to approach these topics.

00:00:27.900 --> 00:00:33.480
Uh, it's just that I wanted to take the time to make sure that I could approach it with the right mindset,

00:00:33.480 --> 00:00:39.120
and I could go into it with the right attitude. A-and, you know, I could take the time to sit down and really

00:00:39.120 --> 00:00:43.420
appreciate every nook and cranny of this game for what it is.

00:00:43.420 --> 00:00:48.900
Because, it's less of a game, and more of an experience because this is based on a true story.

00:00:49.120 --> 00:00:50.820
This is about a family

00:00:51.040 --> 00:00:53.300
whose child has gone through cancer.

00:00:53.300 --> 00:00:56.980
I believe they-their son, at a very young age, they got sick.

00:00:57.120 --> 00:01:02.860
And this is about their story of going through this experience. And I know that many of you out there

00:01:03.120 --> 00:01:07.340
have probably gone through something similar to this, if not you yourself...

00:01:07.640 --> 00:01:09.120
have gone through something...

00:01:09.380 --> 00:01:10.940
to deal with cancer.

00:01:10.940 --> 00:01:13.940
Because it's kind of the one big unifying thing.

00:01:13.940 --> 00:01:18.220
It's the one big unifying tragedy that I think we can all relate to,

00:01:18.360 --> 00:01:20.240
as opposed to just death itself.

00:01:20.240 --> 00:01:24.460
But... Cancer is something that, if you look around in your circle,

00:01:24.460 --> 00:01:27.560
you have a family member or a friend who has been through this,

00:01:27.560 --> 00:01:29.140
and it's an ordeal.

00:01:29.140 --> 00:01:32.880
I-it's more than just the name of what the disease is.

00:01:32.880 --> 00:01:38.800
It's about the entire way that it changes the lives of everyone involved.

00:01:38.800 --> 00:01:43.260
It's a huge subject, and it's something that I wanted to go into,

00:01:43.980 --> 00:01:47.520
and treat with respect. You know, not for my sake.

00:01:47.520 --> 00:01:51.020
Like, it's not about me, it's not about my, you know, experience with it.

00:01:51.020 --> 00:01:56.120
It's about treating this with respect for everyone that has ever gone through something like this.

00:01:56.120 --> 00:02:01.580
So, that being said, this video is going to be a bit different.  It's going to be completely uncut.

00:02:01.580 --> 00:02:05.560
Uh, this video is not monetized, I didn't want to profit off of something like this.

00:02:05.560 --> 00:02:08.340
And uh- I wanted to support the developers as well.

00:02:08.340 --> 00:02:13.660
Uh, I want to make sure that the, um- the uh-h-h, you know,

00:02:13.660 --> 00:02:17.100
the developers get credit for what they have done here.

00:02:17.100 --> 00:02:18.820
And the thing that they have made.

00:02:18.820 --> 00:02:21.460
So, I believe that they have a tip jar, I'll be chipping into that as well.

00:02:21.500 --> 00:02:25.680
And I hope that you guys can reach out to the developers and thank them for making something like this.

00:02:25.740 --> 00:02:27.620
And, uh, it's almost-

00:02:27.620 --> 00:02:29.960
everyone- i-it's critically acclaimed.

00:02:29.960 --> 00:02:33.460
It's a good experience and I know some of you have seen it already,

00:02:33.480 --> 00:02:38.040
and I wanna go into this with like a fresh head, a fresh pair of eyes,

00:02:38.080 --> 00:02:40.860
a completely open understanding of what this life is about,

00:02:40.860 --> 00:02:46.800
because in a game, a game is an experience where usually, typically you have fun-

00:02:46.800 --> 00:02:49.120
Oh, that's a pleasant opening, right on the water.
["Spring Forth" playing in the background]

00:02:49.120 --> 00:02:53.460
Uh, you have fun and you're enjoying yourself and the game itself is...

00:02:53.740 --> 00:02:55.820
the experience for the sake of the experience.

00:02:55.820 --> 00:02:57.600
But this is a story...

00:02:57.860 --> 00:02:59.640
for the sake of a game?

00:02:59.640 --> 00:03:02.300
I don't know if that's even a correct way of putting that but...

00:03:02.640 --> 00:03:05.040
A-at its heart, it's a story,

00:03:05.620 --> 00:03:07.040
and a relatable story.

00:03:07.040 --> 00:03:09.040
Because a game is about immersion-

00:03:09.500 --> 00:03:11.440
 Is this told from the perspective of a duck?

00:03:11.440 --> 00:03:14.760
-uh this game is about immersion, and just like any good story,

00:03:14.760 --> 00:03:17.180
you have to relate to the characters involved.

00:03:17.580 --> 00:03:21.700
And that means approaching it with the right mindset.

00:03:21.700 --> 00:03:23.840
So either way.  I-I'll get into the game now.

00:03:23.840 --> 00:03:25.560
Oh I am a duck.

00:03:25.560 --> 00:03:26.420
Why am I a duck?

00:03:26.420 --> 00:03:28.080
[family talking in the background]
["Feeding the Ducks" playing in the background]

00:03:28.080 --> 00:03:29.840
I'm assuming that's the family I can hear over there.

00:03:29.940 --> 00:03:31.840
[Duck quacks periodically]
Do I--Oh, *imitates duck*

00:03:32.480 --> 00:03:33.140
Yeah.

00:03:33.900 --> 00:03:35.520
Oh, and also you guys may have noticed-

00:03:35.520 --> 00:03:36.820
Hello bread, I'm gonna get you.

00:03:36.960 --> 00:03:39.720
-you guys may have noticed that I'm not in Cincinnati.

00:03:39.720 --> 00:03:44.580
Uh, I was originally gonna be in Cincinnati to do a charity livestream this weekend.

00:03:44.580 --> 00:03:48.040
And I wanted to be able to do that, uh, but unfortunately I didn't have enough time.

00:03:48.040 --> 00:03:50.260
It's, it's the constant curse of my life.

00:03:50.560 --> 00:03:51.260
Um...

00:03:51.620 --> 00:03:56.680
I don't have time, because next week I'm going to San Diego for Comic Con and I just didn't have enough t-

00:03:56.680 --> 00:03:58.820
Oh, sorry, you just tried to eat nothing there.

00:03:59.080 --> 00:03:59.680
Uh...

00:03:59.820 --> 00:04:03.280
I didn't have enough time to go to Cincinnati and see my family and come back,

00:04:03.280 --> 00:04:04.820
which is something that I really wanted to do.

00:04:04.820 --> 00:04:08.040
And I wanted to make this weekend about charity.

00:04:08.040 --> 00:04:13.380
But, thankfully, it already is, because Revelmode is actually doing a charity with Crisis Text Line.

00:04:13.380 --> 00:04:16.660
And I'll put this all in the description below so you can find out more about it.

00:04:16.660 --> 00:04:22.280
And I wanted to also take an opportunity in this game to, you know, raise awareness for that as well.

00:04:23.160 --> 00:04:25.120
So all that's in the- oh.
[Amy - text on-screen]

00:04:25.600 --> 00:04:28.860
So all that's in the description. I'll get into the game now.
[Isaac - text on-screen]

