00:27:08.320 --> 00:27:11.520
I'm not the person who is an expert on art.

00:27:11.520 --> 00:27:12.840
Or what art means.

00:27:12.900 --> 00:27:14.640
And what that stuff means.

00:27:14.640 --> 00:27:20.300
All I'm saying is that this obviously has meaning to the people that go through these experiences.

00:27:20.640 --> 00:27:21.420
And...

00:27:22.000 --> 00:27:25.820
it's just really hard to nail that down.

00:27:26.440 --> 00:27:31.840
I-it's hard to nail it down, like, even to say what's good or bad, in terms of emotions.

00:27:31.840 --> 00:27:33.800
That's why, sometimes, you know,

00:27:33.800 --> 00:27:39.000
you go easy on people that get overly...y'know, antagonistic against art, because...

00:27:39.000 --> 00:27:42.220
Like...i-it's one of the human experiences.

00:27:42.220 --> 00:27:44.340
How do you even comprehend your own emotions?

00:27:44.340 --> 00:27:47.600
Like, how do you comprehend th-the human experiences by yourself?

00:27:47.600 --> 00:27:48.820
There's no guide to it.

00:27:49.000 --> 00:27:50.400
You know, there's no right way, or a wrong way.

00:27:50.400 --> 00:27:51.780
You simply are.

00:27:52.000 --> 00:27:53.200
Yeah, any-anyway...

00:27:53.540 --> 00:27:55.800
Mark: That's enough of me rambling about stuff I don't know about.

00:27:55.800 --> 00:27:57.880
[Amy]

00:28:42.200 --> 00:28:43.120
Amy: Alright, bye.

00:28:43.960 --> 00:28:45.120
Mark: *breathes* Um...

00:28:45.800 --> 00:28:50.000
*sniffs* I wonder if these are the actual paintings in the hospital that they were in.

00:28:50.000 --> 00:28:51.700
Sorry, that got me choked up a little bit...

00:28:52.640 --> 00:28:53.520
I don't know why...

00:28:54.000 --> 00:28:56.380
Anyway... Whoa!

00:28:56.380 --> 00:28:57.420
*chuckling* What...?

00:28:57.420 --> 00:29:00.220
[racing game music playing in the background]
[continuous sound of a race car]

00:29:00.220 --> 00:29:02.320
Oh! *chuckling* Okay...

00:29:03.980 --> 00:29:07.660
Oh, I- *laughing* I am-I... Okay...

00:29:07.660 --> 00:29:10.400
I guess I'm supposed to avoid the giant, fat chicken?

00:29:10.400 --> 00:29:12.100
Whoa, okay.

00:29:12.860 --> 00:29:16.260
*laughing* I am very confused...

00:29:16.620 --> 00:29:18.400
Ohh... I-whoa, hi, sorry about that.

00:29:18.600 --> 00:29:20.520
Sorry, cow.

00:29:21.260 --> 00:29:22.280
I...

00:29:23.380 --> 00:29:24.540
*laughs*

00:29:25.580 --> 00:29:28.820
*laughing* I have no idea what's happening.

00:29:29.540 --> 00:29:30.300
I have no idea- Sorry!

00:29:30.300 --> 00:29:34.320
Ohh man, punted him right out the window... *laughing*

00:29:36.160 --> 00:29:36.660
Ohh man...

00:29:36.660 --> 00:29:38.700
Oh, watch out for the banana.

00:29:39.260 --> 00:29:40.440
Fer da nanner.

00:29:41.000 --> 00:29:41.720
Ohh...

00:29:44.200 --> 00:29:45.400
All roighty then!

00:29:45.400 --> 00:29:47.460
*giggling* Sorry!

00:29:47.840 --> 00:29:49.400
*sniffs* *giggles*

00:29:50.800 --> 00:29:53.000
[victory music]
Oh!  Yay!

00:29:53.220 --> 00:29:56.680
"Lum-" Oh, what is... Oh, I have no idea what all that is.

00:29:57.200 --> 00:29:59.940
Uh, obviously those are all the drugs, that's...

00:30:00.500 --> 00:30:01.500
Man...

00:30:04.100 --> 00:30:05.160
[crash]

00:30:05.160 --> 00:30:06.440
Uh-oh.  Whoa.

00:30:06.440 --> 00:30:08.080
[fun game sounds and music all stop]

00:30:08.080 --> 00:30:09.120
Whoa...

00:30:09.120 --> 00:30:11.520
*sniffs* Okay.  Well, that took a shift.

00:30:11.520 --> 00:30:14.060
Amy: How long will it be before we can have some answers?

00:30:15.000 --> 00:30:16.900
Did anyone ask the doctor?

00:30:17.620 --> 00:30:21.020
Ryan: Okay, is it just the doctor on call, or is this our doctor?

00:30:21.640 --> 00:30:24.420
Well, because the on-call doctor is just a resident...

00:30:26.120 --> 00:30:28.120
Amy: Is there a way we could talk to our doctor?

00:30:28.120 --> 00:30:30.780
[sound of a helicopter passing overhead]

00:30:30.780 --> 00:30:35.660
It just seemed like yesterday, in clinic, they were going to let us go.  I just...want to know what the plan is.

00:30:37.100 --> 00:30:38.820
Ryan: Who cancelled the treatment?

00:30:40.340 --> 00:30:44.040
Amy: I- isn't it dangerous for him not to get it?  I thought he needed that.

00:30:45.120 --> 00:30:51.000
Ryan: I-I know you're just doing what the orders say, but... Can I... Can I just talk to the doctor that ordered it?

00:30:51.000 --> 00:30:54.920
[sirens fade into the background, and then slowly fade out]

00:30:57.940 --> 00:30:58.760
Mark: Hm...

00:31:01.740 --> 00:31:07.780
Man... I-I'm assuming that represents the ups and downs of going through this experience.

00:31:07.780 --> 00:31:09.580
Like, there...there is no...

00:31:11.340 --> 00:31:13.020
...There's not really a happy ending.

00:31:14.040 --> 00:31:19.620
It- just like everything else in life, it's just a series of events, and they can be good or bad.

00:31:21.780 --> 00:31:23.220
And you make the most of it.

00:31:26.300 --> 00:31:31.080
Yeah, I- Maybe this even, too.  Like, the shifting.  Every thingle step I take, it...

00:31:31.320 --> 00:31:33.320
It lights up, and it doesn't light up...

00:31:37.660 --> 00:31:39.660
It goes up and it goes down.

00:31:41.540 --> 00:31:42.380
huh...

00:31:43.900 --> 00:31:45.900
*deep sigh*

00:31:46.840 --> 00:31:47.700
Yeah...

00:31:48.480 --> 00:31:51.340
Ugh, that's so c...complicated.

00:31:51.340 --> 00:31:53.880
It's-it's so complicated!  I-I can't...

00:31:54.240 --> 00:31:59.640
I can't describe it.  And I'm not trying to describe it, I don't-I don't want to describe it.  I want it to be...

00:31:59.860 --> 00:32:05.640
what it is for the sake of what it is, and not for...my interpretation of...what it is.

00:32:06.120 --> 00:32:06.900
Whoa.

00:32:08.540 --> 00:32:10.780
That is...intense.

00:32:10.780 --> 00:32:14.440
[continuous ambient sound]

00:32:14.440 --> 00:32:18.600
And what's even weirder is a lot of these elements here are very familiar to me.

00:32:18.600 --> 00:32:21.260
Because, you know, I've seen all of this first-hand.

00:32:21.260 --> 00:32:25.740
And I know what that machine is in front of me.  It's a targeted radiation therapy machine.

00:32:26.100 --> 00:32:29.380
I know, 'cause I've seen it used on my dad.

00:32:30.440 --> 00:32:31.440
And...

00:32:34.560 --> 00:32:35.360
I don't know.

00:32:36.780 --> 00:32:40.240
I haven't thought about that...thing in years.

00:32:40.240 --> 00:32:45.240
I didn't give that thing a thought since last time I saw it, and now I'm...

00:32:45.240 --> 00:32:47.740
I'm thinking of it, and I can remember that whole day.

00:32:48.220 --> 00:32:51.540
You know, I can remember that whole day.  I remember it, because...

00:32:51.540 --> 00:32:58.100
on the way there, my dad...criticized my driving skills, he told me, you know, I was driving too fast, and...

00:33:00.000 --> 00:33:00.880
You know, that...

00:33:02.000 --> 00:33:05.520
Things like that stick with you, but I...forgot about it.

00:33:09.060 --> 00:33:10.500
Joel: Hey, it's you again!

00:33:10.880 --> 00:33:11.980
I love you!

00:33:11.980 --> 00:33:13.940
[Joel]

00:33:17.580 --> 00:33:18.380
Mark: Oh...

00:33:27.160 --> 00:33:29.260
[Joel laughs]

00:33:34.140 --> 00:33:35.880
Mark: Well, that doesn't sound good...

00:33:36.200 --> 00:33:38.480
I don't think I wanna know about the "big lion."

00:33:38.760 --> 00:33:39.600
Man...

00:33:40.340 --> 00:33:41.300
Alright!

00:33:41.460 --> 00:33:45.740
Joel: He's not a scary lion, but he's so loud.

00:33:45.740 --> 00:33:47.240
Mark: Oh.  How loud?

00:33:50.800 --> 00:33:51.540
Mark: Go for it!

00:33:52.760 --> 00:33:54.080
Mark: That was a pretty scary roar!

00:33:54.080 --> 00:33:58.140
Joel: Don't be afraid.  You might wanna cover your ears.

00:33:58.140 --> 00:33:59.820
Mark: Okay.  I'm on it.

00:34:01.520 --> 00:34:02.640
Oh, he's gettin' ready.

00:34:03.500 --> 00:34:05.160
[lion roars]

00:34:05.760 --> 00:34:09.820
Mark: Wow...  Did he just roar the universe into existence?

00:34:10.460 --> 00:34:11.920
That's really impressive.

00:34:15.060 --> 00:34:20.780
Mark: Little--
[Joel says something about animals and his fravorite?]

00:34:20.780 --> 00:34:22.440
[ambient sound fades into music]

00:34:22.440 --> 00:34:25.280
Mark: ...I didn't understand any of those words.  What did you say?

00:34:25.280 --> 00:34:27.840
["And God Saw That It Was Good" playing in the background]

00:34:32.280 --> 00:34:34.280
What is this?  Oh, what am I doing?

00:34:34.800 --> 00:34:36.760
What am I- Ohhh...

00:34:39.600 --> 00:34:44.360
Ohh, these are the constellations.  Oh, okay.

00:34:45.060 --> 00:34:46.060
[Joel laughs]

00:34:46.060 --> 00:34:47.520
That's the horse.

00:34:48.000 --> 00:34:49.940
This is, um...

00:34:50.280 --> 00:34:52.320
A giraffe, apparently.

00:34:52.700 --> 00:34:56.840
And this is, ummmmmm, the lion?
[Joel laughs]

00:34:56.840 --> 00:35:00.340
Nope.  That's another poochie.  Ohh, he was on the ram.

00:35:01.080 --> 00:35:03.720
Okay, so I j- I guess I just gotta get all these...

00:35:04.920 --> 00:35:08.560
constellations properly engaged...?

00:35:08.560 --> 00:35:11.660
[Joel laughs]

00:35:11.660 --> 00:35:13.660
Ohhh, okay.

00:35:13.660 --> 00:35:15.460
I think he's gotta ride on all of them.

00:35:15.460 --> 00:35:16.640
[Joel laughs]

00:35:16.840 --> 00:35:20.140
Go for the- go for the giraffe, it's...obviously better.

00:35:20.540 --> 00:35:21.960
Well, probably not better than the dog.

00:35:21.960 --> 00:35:25.280
I don't know if the giraffe can do backflips, but I'm gonna try my best here.

00:35:28.420 --> 00:35:29.500
Huh...

00:35:29.740 --> 00:35:32.060
How 'bout go for- yeah!  There ya go!

00:35:33.140 --> 00:35:34.680
That would be my favorite.

00:35:36.520 --> 00:35:38.160
I think the horsey's gonna be next.

00:35:41.700 --> 00:35:43.500
[Joel laughs]
Heh...

00:35:44.900 --> 00:35:45.720
Yeah...

00:35:48.780 --> 00:35:51.820
[Joel laughs]
I'm just, um...

00:35:52.000 --> 00:35:54.440
I'm just trying to ponder...

00:35:55.520 --> 00:35:56.580
the meaning.

00:35:56.760 --> 00:35:59.540
'Ca-that's all I'm trying to do when I'm- when I'm seeing this.

00:35:59.540 --> 00:36:04.940
I'm trying to open my mind to what the meaning of this is, and I'm not entirely sure what the meaning...

00:36:04.940 --> 00:36:10.600
behind this scene is, because I guarantee you that each scene in this game is a representation of...

00:36:10.600 --> 00:36:12.000
[Amy singing in the background]

00:36:12.000 --> 00:36:14.600
the life of everyone that has gone through this.

00:36:15.480 --> 00:36:16.680
Joel included.

00:36:16.920 --> 00:36:20.200
So, I gotta remember that some things might be from Joel's perspective.

00:36:20.200 --> 00:36:20.880
[sound fades out]

00:36:20.880 --> 00:36:23.520
Or at least their interpretation of what that means.
[sound fades out]

00:36:23.840 --> 00:36:24.600
You know.

00:36:26.800 --> 00:36:27.600
Anyway...

00:36:27.600 --> 00:36:30.500
[Amy humming "How Great Thou Art" distantly in the background]

00:36:42.200 --> 00:36:47.260
[Amy's humming becomes less distant and more present, and continues in the background]

00:36:48.880 --> 00:36:50.880
Mark: That's a lot of cards...

00:36:52.920 --> 00:36:56.120
"Elsie, we love you dearly and miss you daily, see you s..." *chokes up*

00:37:00.980 --> 00:37:03.960
[muffled voice on intercom]

00:37:03.960 --> 00:37:06.280
*reads text on card*

00:37:07.660 --> 00:37:09.660
Did I start at the wrong end?

00:37:11.060 --> 00:37:12.500
Let me start over here.

00:37:14.200 --> 00:37:15.600
*sighs*

00:37:17.480 --> 00:37:20.920
[muffled voice on intercom]

00:37:31.860 --> 00:37:33.740
*sniffs* Oh, whoops.

00:37:34.340 --> 00:37:35.960
*swallows and exhales*

00:37:35.960 --> 00:37:38.080
I think I know what these cards are...

00:37:42.060 --> 00:37:45.940
[muffled voice on intercom]

00:37:50.560 --> 00:37:52.020
*choked* Four...

00:37:59.200 --> 00:38:01.880
*crying softly*

00:38:03.360 --> 00:38:04.440
*sniffs*

00:38:05.220 --> 00:38:06.700
Sorry... Hang on.

00:38:06.700 --> 00:38:07.680
[muffled voice on intercom]

00:38:07.680 --> 00:38:09.880
Ahhh, sorry sorry sorry.
[muffled voice on intercom]

00:38:11.540 --> 00:38:13.240
Ah, sorry sorry sorry...

00:38:14.560 --> 00:38:16.940
*sniffs, and sighs deeply*

00:38:25.140 --> 00:38:27.260
*choked* That's a lot of cards.

00:38:28.100 --> 00:38:30.780
[muffled voice on intercom]

00:38:43.120 --> 00:38:45.480
*still choked* Oh, it's so many cards...

00:38:47.020 --> 00:38:51.640
[muffled voice on intercom]

00:38:51.640 --> 00:38:55.580
Oh man... I don't know if I'm gonna be able to get through all of these...

00:38:56.160 --> 00:38:57.080
*sniffs*

00:39:00.260 --> 00:39:01.460
Ohh, man...

00:39:02.600 --> 00:39:03.820
Oh, I have to walk?

00:39:03.820 --> 00:39:05.400
[muffled voice on intercom]

00:39:05.400 --> 00:39:06.460
Hang on...
[muffled voice on intercom]

00:39:06.460 --> 00:39:08.800
[Amy's humming stops]

00:39:08.800 --> 00:39:11.200
[Amy]

00:39:32.160 --> 00:39:33.280
*sniffs*

00:39:54.980 --> 00:39:56.720
*sighs*
[muffled voice on intercom]

00:39:56.720 --> 00:39:58.360
[muffled voice on intercom]

00:39:58.360 --> 00:40:00.140
That's a lot of handprints...

00:40:02.820 --> 00:40:06.500
I hope you guys aren't waiting for me to have words of wisdom here, I...I...

00:40:06.820 --> 00:40:09.500
I don't quite have...um...

00:40:11.760 --> 00:40:13.980
*sniffs* I don't quite have, uh...

00:40:15.760 --> 00:40:17.400
You know, my thoughts together.

00:40:17.480 --> 00:40:19.340
Oh, sorry.  I already read that one.

00:40:19.420 --> 00:40:21.420
There's so many cards.

00:40:22.680 --> 00:40:24.520
There's SO many cards.

00:40:25.320 --> 00:40:26.060
*sniffs*

00:40:35.160 --> 00:40:37.200
Oh, man, there's so many cards.

00:40:37.400 --> 00:40:38.840
I don't wanna miss any.

00:40:45.560 --> 00:40:47.740
These are all just goodbyes.

00:40:49.420 --> 00:40:50.300
Yeah...

00:40:50.620 --> 00:40:53.000
I wanna hit every one of these.  I do.

00:40:53.900 --> 00:40:54.760
'Cause...

00:40:56.540 --> 00:40:58.760
'Cause what's fascinating is...

00:41:00.280 --> 00:41:04.960
And especially here, in representation of this, and this may...seem...

00:41:06.260 --> 00:41:08.340
This may seem trivial to go through each of these.

00:41:08.780 --> 00:41:11.980
But...the important thing to remember is...

00:41:14.000 --> 00:41:19.720
that...in all of this...in every one of these cards...

00:41:20.020 --> 00:41:25.500
It may be a short...little, few words, and it may not seem like much, but...

00:41:26.080 --> 00:41:28.800
This entire game...is about one person.

00:41:28.800 --> 00:41:31.560
["Awake, Oh Awake My Joel" playing in the background]

00:41:31.560 --> 00:41:33.280
It's about ONE.

00:41:34.840 --> 00:41:36.700
And, each of these cards...

00:41:37.520 --> 00:41:38.900
is about another person.

00:41:42.120 --> 00:41:43.080
So...

00:41:43.900 --> 00:41:45.460
To know that...

00:41:48.100 --> 00:41:50.140
*getting choked again* That every single card here...

00:41:51.700 --> 00:41:55.200
is just a small piece of someone else's life...

00:41:57.700 --> 00:41:58.600
Oh...

00:41:59.000 --> 00:42:01.500
*tearful chuckle* I don't think I can get to all the cards...

00:42:02.680 --> 00:42:04.680
*sniffs* But, to know...

00:42:05.180 --> 00:42:07.260
that each of these- Oops.  Eh...

00:42:07.980 --> 00:42:10.400
is another piece of someone's life...

00:42:16.180 --> 00:42:17.920
*choked* You know, that's important.

00:42:19.480 --> 00:42:24.560
It's important to know that...every single person who's gone through something like this...

00:42:25.280 --> 00:42:29.960
They've had an experience much like this game, and what this game is,

00:42:29.960 --> 00:42:32.620
and they've had an experience much like what...

00:42:33.880 --> 00:42:36.380
the family of Joel has gone through.

00:42:40.260 --> 00:42:42.180
And that's just important to remember.

00:42:42.180 --> 00:42:45.500
And these small tokens, you know- and there's so many!

00:42:49.140 --> 00:42:50.780
*choked* Oh, there's so many.

00:42:52.480 --> 00:42:55.920
Ohh, there's so many... How do you- How do you pick which ones?

00:42:59.840 --> 00:43:02.800
But, that's something to hold true to other things.

00:43:05.320 --> 00:43:06.080
You know...

00:43:06.480 --> 00:43:09.400
'Cause there are, i-it's not all tragedy.

00:43:09.520 --> 00:43:14.260
There are some success stories with cancer, and it's getting better every year.

00:43:14.740 --> 00:43:17.680
And hopefully, one day, you know, we'll be able to put...

00:43:19.100 --> 00:43:23.160
you know, this sort of thing behind us.  Not that we'll ever be able to defeat death, or...

00:43:23.300 --> 00:43:25.040
Uh, I don't think we will.

00:43:25.440 --> 00:43:29.180
You know, and I don't even know if that's a goal that everyone should have, but...

00:43:29.820 --> 00:43:30.580
*sniffs*

00:43:34.940 --> 00:43:35.780
You know...

00:43:41.040 --> 00:43:41.920
It's all about...

00:43:44.120 --> 00:43:47.100
you know, learning to see things in perspective.

00:43:48.240 --> 00:43:53.120
For everyone involved.  Everyone who's been through something like this, everyone who has...

00:43:55.180 --> 00:43:56.460
seen this...

00:43:57.380 --> 00:44:00.660
Anyway.  I'm getting to that rambly part again, but...

00:44:00.980 --> 00:44:03.940
I th-I hope...I hope I made...my point.

00:44:05.520 --> 00:44:07.400
And I think this is a good card to end on.

00:44:10.240 --> 00:44:11.360
There's just so many.

00:44:13.280 --> 00:44:15.280
A-and I think...you know...

00:44:16.120 --> 00:44:18.200
I wish I could get to all these, but...

00:44:18.980 --> 00:44:22.320
It would take...a long time.

00:44:25.680 --> 00:44:27.860
*sigh*

00:44:28.000 --> 00:44:30.600
*choked* Now I feel guilty turning my back on some of these.

00:44:31.480 --> 00:44:33.480
*sniffs and exhales vocally*

00:44:34.980 --> 00:44:35.480
*sighs*

00:44:37.540 --> 00:44:39.660
Man...so many- Oh.

00:44:39.660 --> 00:44:42.280
[Muffled voices in the background]

00:44:44.700 --> 00:44:47.000
*deep sigh*

00:44:47.000 --> 00:44:47.800
[music and voices fade]

00:44:47.800 --> 00:44:50.700
And, admittedly, like...you know...
[music and voices fade]

00:44:52.540 --> 00:44:53.180
Oh...

00:44:54.540 --> 00:44:56.640
Eh, that wasn't an important thought anyway.

00:44:57.520 --> 00:44:58.480
Sorry...

00:45:02.460 --> 00:45:04.320
Oh, are you pointing where I should be looking?

00:45:04.320 --> 00:45:06.080
Joel: More? *laughs*
Mark: Tha-thanks, Joel.

00:45:06.680 --> 00:45:07.660
*laughs softly*

00:45:08.380 --> 00:45:09.180
Oh.

00:45:09.940 --> 00:45:11.160
Oh, okay.

00:45:11.520 --> 00:45:12.300
Huh...

00:45:12.520 --> 00:45:14.460
Joel: *small laugh* ...More?
Mark: Okay.

00:45:14.580 --> 00:45:15.420
Alright.

00:45:16.040 --> 00:45:17.020
How 'bout the cow?

00:45:18.660 --> 00:45:19.460
No?

00:45:23.320 --> 00:45:24.400
Ahh, there we go.

00:45:24.960 --> 00:45:26.960
[See-N-Say toy - text on-screen]

00:45:27.420 --> 00:45:28.480
[Joel laughs]

00:45:28.480 --> 00:45:29.640
Mark: ...Why??

00:45:35.200 --> 00:45:36.940
Ahhh...
[Joel laughs]

00:45:37.140 --> 00:45:39.900
That's...weird things for Farmer Bill to do.

00:45:42.860 --> 00:45:43.920
Uh, again...

00:45:44.460 --> 00:45:45.820
[Joel giggles]
Hm...

00:45:45.820 --> 00:45:48.140
That both- says two things about Farmer Bill.

00:45:52.320 --> 00:45:53.380
[Joel giggles]

00:45:53.960 --> 00:45:54.980
...Huuh.

00:45:55.900 --> 00:45:57.100
Interesting.

00:46:00.660 --> 00:46:03.420
[Joel laughs]
Oooh!  Fancy!

00:46:03.780 --> 00:46:05.780
The horse seems the most interesting.

00:46:08.180 --> 00:46:09.120
Yeah, that horse-

00:46:10.000 --> 00:46:14.040
The horse seems pretty smart.  Admittedly, I think that's actually appropriate in this scenario.

00:46:14.120 --> 00:46:16.760
This bizarre experience thing that I'm...going through.

00:46:18.260 --> 00:46:20.300
[Joel laughs]
What polite pigs.

00:46:24.840 --> 00:46:25.640
Tha-

00:46:29.200 --> 00:46:30.240
...Okay.

00:46:30.440 --> 00:46:32.220
Th-this is a weird toy.

00:46:32.680 --> 00:46:33.300
I-I-I-

00:46:33.300 --> 00:46:35.300
[Doctor - text on-screen]

00:46:35.880 --> 00:46:37.260
["I'm Sorry Guys, It's Not Good" plays in the background]

00:46:37.260 --> 00:46:39.260
Mark: ...Well, that was the name of the...chapter.
["I'm Sorry Guys, It's Not Good" plays in the background]

00:46:40.100 --> 00:46:42.160
Oh...wow.

00:46:43.040 --> 00:46:44.440
What is this?

00:46:49.960 --> 00:46:51.960
[Ryan]

00:46:53.080 --> 00:46:55.080
[Doctor talking indistinctly in the background]

00:47:03.740 --> 00:47:05.460
Doctor: -it's quite small at this point,

00:47:05.460 --> 00:47:07.460
[Doctor]

00:47:17.940 --> 00:47:20.600
Mark: *deep breath*

00:47:25.000 --> 00:47:26.000
[Amy]

00:47:28.780 --> 00:47:30.700
[Doctor talking in the background]

00:47:31.520 --> 00:47:35.260
Doctor: ...it is fatal.  It's only a matter of time before...

00:47:38.160 --> 00:47:40.160
...we've already thrown all the chemotherapy...

00:47:41.620 --> 00:47:44.640
...can't continue to give him chemotherapy that we know he's resistant to...

00:48:06.840 --> 00:48:08.840
[Doctor]

00:48:11.220 --> 00:48:12.160
Mark: Oh, man...

00:48:12.600 --> 00:48:16.880
And that's the fascinating thing, like there's no-there's no right way to respond to it.

00:48:16.880 --> 00:48:19.720
Everyone responds to terrible news differently.

00:48:20.120 --> 00:48:25.080
Like...I remember the first time that I heard that my dad had cancer.

00:48:26.280 --> 00:48:29.760
That's a...that's a personal story I don't think I'm gonna go into.

00:48:29.760 --> 00:48:31.840
[Nurse - text on-screen]

00:48:40.160 --> 00:48:44.000
Mark: *breathes*

00:48:48.760 --> 00:48:51.800
[Doctor]
[Doctor also still talking indistinctly in the background]

00:48:54.800 --> 00:48:56.020
Doctor: ...palliative treatment...

00:48:57.840 --> 00:48:59.840
[Nurse talking in the background]

00:49:01.720 --> 00:49:03.500
Nurse: ...to improve the quality of life...

00:49:11.220 --> 00:49:13.140
Doctor: -talk to our radiation oncologist, to decide whether

00:49:13.140 --> 00:49:15.140
[Doctor]

00:49:16.380 --> 00:49:17.520
[Ryan]

00:49:18.460 --> 00:49:20.120
[Doctor]

00:49:22.320 --> 00:49:25.500
[The sound of rain is gradually growing louder in the background]

00:49:30.720 --> 00:49:31.860
Mark: *exhales*

00:49:34.140 --> 00:49:35.600
It's not time yet...

00:49:36.800 --> 00:49:39.420
Ahh... Oh, man.

00:49:39.760 --> 00:49:40.720
Sorry.

00:49:42.160 --> 00:49:44.160
I'm a disgusting slob.
[Ryan]

00:49:45.140 --> 00:49:47.220
[same conversation repeats indistinctly in the background]

00:50:35.920 --> 00:50:38.000
Ryan: ...and when doctors can't. [text on-screen]

00:50:41.200 --> 00:50:42.180
Doctor: [text on-screen]

00:50:49.240 --> 00:50:50.700
Mark: Oh, man...

00:50:53.160 --> 00:50:55.160
Amy: [text on-screen]

00:51:11.800 --> 00:51:14.140
[sound of rushing water getting louder, thunder starting]

00:51:14.520 --> 00:51:17.040
[conversation echoing distantly back-and-forth]

00:51:22.900 --> 00:51:23.780
Mark: Man...

00:51:31.620 --> 00:51:33.360
Oh, this is so weird.

00:51:36.020 --> 00:51:36.600
I...

00:51:42.620 --> 00:51:44.240
I'll hold it.  I'll save it.

00:52:03.980 --> 00:52:06.660
That's...that's so weird...

00:52:08.700 --> 00:52:10.700
[conversation is drowned out by the sound of the storm]

00:52:14.300 --> 00:52:15.480
Again, I'm not...

00:52:17.080 --> 00:52:22.320
I'm not the best to interpret what other people feel in certain circumstances...

00:52:22.740 --> 00:52:27.840
But I wonder if this is their interpretation of Joel's perspective on all this.

00:52:28.420 --> 00:52:32.840
'Cause a lot of this game has been about perspective, and seeing things from other perspectives,

00:52:32.840 --> 00:52:38.000
and understanding that...each person responds differently, and they respond in a variety of ways,

00:52:38.000 --> 00:52:40.380
and where they- Whoa, wha...what am I looking at?

00:52:40.900 --> 00:52:42.360
Whoa.  What-?

00:52:43.100 --> 00:52:44.440
I-I think I ran in-...

00:52:44.600 --> 00:52:46.280
Oh.  Nevermind.

00:52:46.800 --> 00:52:51.960
Anyway... I-i-it's just like, people respond in different ways, and just because someone responds one way

00:52:51.960 --> 00:52:56.060
initially, doesn't mean that that's...how they're gonna respond later, or...

00:52:56.500 --> 00:52:57.940
that's what they really mean.

00:52:59.300 --> 00:53:00.220
I don't know...

00:53:04.760 --> 00:53:07.560
It's another thing about...talking about hope.

00:53:07.680 --> 00:53:09.580
Talking about what hope there is, and...

00:53:10.180 --> 00:53:13.520
the hope you have in terms of situtations like this, and...

00:53:13.920 --> 00:53:16.080
And what hope can do, you know?

00:53:17.240 --> 00:53:19.840
'Cause, what can hope do?  Hope can do nothing...

00:53:22.100 --> 00:53:25.520
Nothing, except...make people feel.

00:53:26.260 --> 00:53:29.160
Hope is just another thing that makes people feel something.

00:53:30.300 --> 00:53:32.220
Maybe hope is art, I don't know...

00:53:34.060 --> 00:53:34.980
*sighs*

00:53:38.000 --> 00:53:39.240
Oh, man...

00:53:40.120 --> 00:53:42.280
Now, I believe I'm the bird?  I believe?

00:53:44.120 --> 00:53:46.120
Is there something else I'm supposed to see first?

00:53:46.220 --> 00:53:46.960
Nah...

00:53:51.340 --> 00:53:53.340
Mark: "I have-" oh.
Amy: [reads letter on-screen]

00:54:59.320 --> 00:55:00.220
Mark: Hm...

00:55:02.260 --> 00:55:03.060
Yeah...

00:55:03.920 --> 00:55:06.440
A-and some people turn to religion for...

00:55:06.620 --> 00:55:11.900
times like this.  I mean, that's just another thing, that everyone deals in crisises in their own way.

00:55:12.400 --> 00:55:14.160
Like, who's to judge?

00:55:14.840 --> 00:55:16.840
Who's to say one, more than another?

00:55:18.200 --> 00:55:21.300
[voices fading in]
Ryan: Guys, are you ready for bed?

00:55:21.300 --> 00:55:23.740
Amy:  Joel.  Lay.  Down.

00:55:25.080 --> 00:55:27.760
Okay.  Should we do a song?

00:55:27.760 --> 00:55:28.880
Ryan: Oh, sure.

00:55:28.880 --> 00:55:33.060
Amy: Okay.  Uhh, big boys?  How 'bout you come in here, and we'll sing the littles a lullaby.

00:55:33.540 --> 00:55:34.600
Isaac: I'm tired...

00:55:34.600 --> 00:55:37.140
Amy: *laughs* I know, it's-it's bedtime.

00:55:37.660 --> 00:55:42.020
Ohh, okay... [indistinct] Lay down.

00:55:42.220 --> 00:55:44.480
Mark: Whoa.  Where are you going?

00:55:45.240 --> 00:55:47.760
[converstion continuing in background]

00:55:47.760 --> 00:55:50.180
Mark: Whoa... Ohh, that's the lighthouse!

00:55:51.700 --> 00:55:52.640
Huhh...

00:55:52.640 --> 00:55:54.640
[conversation fades out]

00:55:55.000 --> 00:55:55.760
Mark: Huh.

00:55:57.180 --> 00:55:57.980
Man...

00:55:58.400 --> 00:56:01.160
An-and it's also- It's also bizarre.

00:56:01.880 --> 00:56:05.940
Like, once you find out that... cancer is terminal, like-

00:56:05.940 --> 00:56:07.540
Amy: [reads letter on-screen]

00:57:12.140 --> 00:57:12.960
Mark: Yeah...

00:57:13.440 --> 00:57:16.560
Anyway, to finish what I was saying, and start another thought, is...

00:57:17.440 --> 00:57:22.960
It's-it's a-it's an interesting conundrum, when you find out the cancer is fatal, because...

00:57:23.620 --> 00:57:27.480
You-you get that bombshell of knowledge, and then what do you do with it?

00:57:27.480 --> 00:57:31.800
You-you walk about your normal life, until you eventually die.

00:57:32.100 --> 00:57:34.440
Like...i-that's a blunt way to say it...

00:57:34.780 --> 00:57:37.680
But that's literally the experience, like...

00:57:37.880 --> 00:57:44.340
What do you do, after you're told that you're gonna die?  I've never faced this myself, but...  You know, that...

00:57:45.540 --> 00:57:47.040
That's what happens.

00:57:47.880 --> 00:57:51.900
And then you have to continue on, and find joy in-in whatever you can.

00:57:53.040 --> 00:57:53.820
Yeah...

00:57:54.000 --> 00:57:57.720
And I have another thought...later on, but... I'll get to it; I'll probably forget it.

00:57:57.720 --> 00:57:59.720
Man: [reads letter on-screen]

00:58:52.400 --> 00:58:56.360
Mark: Hm... So, these are notes from...other people in the hospital, too?

00:58:56.960 --> 00:58:58.540
Is every bottle a note?

00:58:58.540 --> 00:59:02.060
Oh... No, every bot- some of those bottles are like baby bottles, I believe.

00:59:02.760 --> 00:59:04.200
I don't think they're all notes.

00:59:04.720 --> 00:59:05.540
Anyway...

00:59:05.980 --> 00:59:10.160
Yeah, I-I can't- I can't remember what my other thought was.  I-it probably wasn't very important.

00:59:10.160 --> 00:59:12.160
Just like the majority of my thoughts during this.

00:59:12.160 --> 00:59:14.340
Caleb: So, how long are we gonna be in California?

00:59:14.340 --> 00:59:19.900
Mark: Hm...
Amy: Um... hmph.  I don't actually know, that's kind of why we're packing up everything.

00:59:19.900 --> 00:59:26.320
Amy: It's because... if the trial works really well, then maybe we'll stay in California for a really long time,

00:59:26.320 --> 00:59:30.320
Like, as long as it keeps helping Joel, then we want to stay, and do the best we can for him,

00:59:30.320 --> 00:59:32.160
and stay there where he's getting help.

00:59:32.420 --> 00:59:37.220
But, if the medicine starts to not work, as soon as it's not helping him, I promise we'll come back home.

00:59:37.220 --> 00:59:40.660
Caleb: Oh... Are we going to Disneyland?

00:59:40.660 --> 00:59:42.140
Ryan: Yeah, of course.

00:59:42.140 --> 00:59:44.120
Mark: *laughs quietly* The important question.

00:59:44.120 --> 00:59:46.120
Ryan: [indistinct]

00:59:46.120 --> 00:59:49.500
Caleb: I'm kind of excited, but I'm kind of not...

00:59:50.800 --> 00:59:53.180
I mean, I think it'll be fun, but...

00:59:54.680 --> 00:59:56.540
I just don't like missing school.

00:59:56.540 --> 00:59:58.080
Amy: *laughs* Oh, yeah...

00:59:58.080 --> 01:00:01.000
Ryan: *laughs* You're the only 8-year-old to ever say that.

01:00:01.000 --> 01:00:02.240
Mark: *laughs*

01:00:02.240 --> 01:00:04.040
Ryan: That's amazing.
Amy: I hate to miss the [indistinct]

01:00:04.040 --> 01:00:06.940
Mark: Yeah... I dunno about that one...

01:00:08.220 --> 01:00:09.900
Oh, there's so many notes.

01:00:10.240 --> 01:00:12.240
Amy: [reads letter on-screen]

01:01:39.640 --> 01:01:40.540
Mark: Hm...

01:01:41.700 --> 01:01:43.200
Ohh, man.

01:01:47.800 --> 01:01:49.880
Amy: [reads letter on-screen]

01:02:12.360 --> 01:02:14.200
Julianne: [reads letter on-screen]

01:03:39.160 --> 01:03:41.960
Mark: *sniffs and exhales* Man...

01:03:43.800 --> 01:03:46.560
I don't know if I'm gonna be able to get to all the notes in the- Whooa...

01:03:47.260 --> 01:03:48.840
I didn't expect that...

01:03:51.760 --> 01:03:53.040
Man... it's-

01:03:53.040 --> 01:03:54.940
Ryan: [text on-screen]

01:03:58.480 --> 01:04:00.860
Ryan: Do you know what she wrote on the eve of Joel's first surgery?

01:04:01.380 --> 01:04:03.880
The one back in January, when we first found the tumor?

01:04:05.080 --> 01:04:07.860
"I seriously feel like a kid on Christmas Eve."

01:04:10.540 --> 01:04:12.540
[text on-screen]

01:04:20.140 --> 01:04:23.140
And yet my wife is expecting a surprise party from the Lord.

01:04:23.660 --> 01:04:25.140
Replete with presents.

01:04:25.140 --> 01:04:27.140
[text on-screen]

01:04:35.220 --> 01:04:35.880
Mark: Yeah...

01:04:37.020 --> 01:04:41.180
And then, the counterpart.  Some people can't turn to religion.

01:04:41.500 --> 01:04:43.420
Some people... I-I'm not saying...

01:04:43.740 --> 01:04:47.040
commenting on anyone's religious beliefs, that's not what I'm doing.  I'm saying...

01:04:47.040 --> 01:04:51.460
Some people approach crisis logically...you know.

01:04:51.700 --> 01:04:56.160
Some people want to put hope in other things.  Some people want to try to control it.

01:04:56.160 --> 01:04:59.100
I mean...there...there's no correct way.

01:04:59.100 --> 01:05:00.960
"Joel the Baby Knight" *laughs*

01:05:01.660 --> 01:05:03.660
Amy: [text on game screen]

01:05:05.060 --> 01:05:07.060
Ryan: [text on game screen]

01:05:07.660 --> 01:05:09.660
Caleb: Ohh... [text on game screen]

01:05:15.000 --> 01:05:15.880
Mark: Okay.

01:05:16.620 --> 01:05:17.900
Ryan: *sighs* Sure.
Mark: Ohh...

01:05:17.900 --> 01:05:19.600
Amy: [text on-screen]

01:05:25.760 --> 01:05:27.000
Mark: Uh-huh...

01:05:27.000 --> 01:05:28.700
[applause]
Mark: Ohhhh!

01:05:28.700 --> 01:05:29.940
Isaac: [text on-screen]
Mark: Hi~i! *chuckles*

01:05:29.940 --> 01:05:32.420
Joel: *laughs*
Ryan: [text on-screen]

01:05:34.220 --> 01:05:36.380
[trumpet fanfare]

01:05:36.380 --> 01:05:37.560
Mark: Uh-huh.

01:05:39.380 --> 01:05:40.540
Mark: Uh oh.

01:05:41.880 --> 01:05:42.760
Huh...

01:05:45.020 --> 01:05:46.740
Heh... Awww...

01:05:46.740 --> 01:05:47.800
Caleb: [text on-screen]

01:05:47.800 --> 01:05:48.620
Ryan: [text on-screen]

01:05:50.660 --> 01:05:52.160
Isaac: [text on-screen]

01:05:52.160 --> 01:05:54.000
Ryan: [text on-screen]

01:05:54.920 --> 01:05:56.580
Mark: Euggh, why am-
Isaac: [text on-screen]

01:05:56.740 --> 01:05:59.540
Ryan: [text on-screen]
Mark: *laughs* Why am I walking- Oookay...

01:05:59.740 --> 01:06:01.480
Mark: Why am I walking towards it?
Isaac: [text on-screen]

01:06:01.480 --> 01:06:02.100
Mark: W-ooh!

01:06:02.880 --> 01:06:05.260
Mark: I ducked!
Ryan: [text on-screen]

01:06:05.260 --> 01:06:06.560
Mark: *laughs* So much fire...

01:06:06.820 --> 01:06:08.080
I ducked...

01:06:10.820 --> 01:06:11.600
Oop!

01:06:13.140 --> 01:06:15.140
Caleb: [text on-screen]

01:06:17.440 --> 01:06:19.440
Isaac: [text on-screen]

01:06:20.980 --> 01:06:22.980
Ryan: [text on-screen]

01:06:23.400 --> 01:06:24.700
Mark: Whoa, whoops.

01:06:24.700 --> 01:06:25.500
Uh-oh!

01:06:25.500 --> 01:06:26.900
Ah, I didn't know that was coming.

01:06:27.220 --> 01:06:29.220
Ryan: [text on-screen]

01:06:40.200 --> 01:06:42.560
Isaac: [text on-screen]
Mark: Ehhhh~

01:06:42.560 --> 01:06:44.560
Ryan: [text on-screen]

01:06:46.100 --> 01:06:48.100
Caleb: [text on-screen]

01:06:48.200 --> 01:06:50.200
Ryan: [text on-screen]

01:06:50.200 --> 01:06:52.200
Mark: Ahhh!
Amy: [text on-screen]

01:06:52.280 --> 01:06:54.280
Caleb: [text on-screen]

01:06:54.900 --> 01:06:56.440
Ryan: [text on-screen]

01:06:56.440 --> 01:06:59.020
Mark: Kinda like help.  Yeah, close.  Close enough.

01:06:59.260 --> 01:07:00.260
Ya did good.

01:07:00.900 --> 01:07:04.760
Ryan: You know, and he's not the only one who's ever tried to fight this dragon.

01:07:05.160 --> 01:07:08.360
Some very brave knights have fought this dragon, and lost.

01:07:08.680 --> 01:07:14.060
And, some are able to drive the dragon off, and then they can go home, and they can quit fighting for a while.

01:07:14.060 --> 01:07:16.060
Ryan: And the kingdom is safe.
Mark: Hehh...

01:07:16.060 --> 01:07:19.800
Amy: Joel's been fighting this dragon for a long time, huh?

01:07:19.800 --> 01:07:22.200
Isaac: A looong time.

01:07:22.920 --> 01:07:29.900
Amy: But...Joel found a nice, empty cave...where he could rest.

01:07:30.380 --> 01:07:33.540
And it seemed like the dragon couldn't find him.

01:07:33.540 --> 01:07:41.700
But just when he thought that the danger was past, the dragon found his hiding spot, and came after him, in the cave!

01:07:41.700 --> 01:07:45.600
Mark: Uh-oh!
Isaac: [text on-screen]

01:07:45.600 --> 01:07:47.100
Amy: [text on-screen]

01:07:47.100 --> 01:07:49.100
Isaac: [text on-screen]

01:07:51.500 --> 01:07:52.820
Mark: Heh, you'll see about that!

01:07:53.060 --> 01:07:55.060
Amy: [text on-screen]

01:08:14.040 --> 01:08:14.760
Mark: Huuh...

01:08:19.140 --> 01:08:22.140
Hyeh!  Byuh!  Hyugh!  Huh!  Uh-oh!

01:08:24.200 --> 01:08:28.340
I think th-I think I'm in some sort of a sweet spot, that I'm not gonna get much damage over here.

01:08:28.420 --> 01:08:29.680
Shoobidee, shoobidoo.

01:08:29.680 --> 01:08:32.280
Whoa, tricksy!  Tricksy, are ya?

01:08:32.400 --> 01:08:33.840
Oh- Ahh!  Oh no!

01:08:33.840 --> 01:08:35.840
Noo!  Don't make me start over!

01:08:35.840 --> 01:08:37.160
Caleb: [text on-screen]

01:08:37.160 --> 01:08:38.480
Mark: I almost had that!

01:08:40.220 --> 01:08:41.620
Awww, I had that.

01:08:44.360 --> 01:08:46.360
Mark: I had that!
Amy: [text on-screen]

01:08:50.400 --> 01:08:52.640
Mark: Ohhh, I-I don't think I could've won.

01:09:09.820 --> 01:09:11.660
Oh, I see, I can just crouch.  Eh!

01:09:11.800 --> 01:09:15.460
Eh!  Eh!  Eh!  Ehh!  Ehh!  Eh!

01:09:15.460 --> 01:09:16.500
Come at me, dragon!

01:09:16.640 --> 01:09:18.260
Whoa!  That's not what I meant to do.

01:09:20.500 --> 01:09:25.060
Huh.  I don't think anyone can beat this dragon, I think it's just about getting the high score.

01:09:25.660 --> 01:09:27.300
Heeey, ya foolish fool.

01:09:40.060 --> 01:09:45.600
Yeah, I don't think there's a way to win this, so I think the only way to progress is probably to lose.

01:09:46.840 --> 01:09:48.020
If I had to guess...

01:09:50.080 --> 01:09:51.000
Hueh!

01:09:58.900 --> 01:09:59.520
Hmm...

01:10:04.660 --> 01:10:06.200
This is fascinating...

01:10:06.400 --> 01:10:11.100
It-it really is!  Like, I'm not even joking about that.  It's-it-this is legitimately fascinating.

01:10:11.720 --> 01:10:14.360
All of it is.  I might have missed that entirely.

01:10:14.500 --> 01:10:16.980
'Cause I-I wouldn't have looked at the ring.  I almost didn't.

01:10:17.740 --> 01:10:19.180
So I guess I can get outta here.

01:10:20.320 --> 01:10:22.440
Oh, there's a bite taken outta that preserver.

01:10:24.360 --> 01:10:25.260
Yeah...

01:10:25.580 --> 01:10:26.900
Kay, where am I headed?

01:10:28.320 --> 01:10:29.740
Ovah, heaah?

01:10:29.740 --> 01:10:31.480
Oh, that's a lot of notes.

01:10:31.720 --> 01:10:33.040
There's a lot of notes.

01:10:35.800 --> 01:10:36.740
Huh...

01:10:37.280 --> 01:10:38.380
Ryan: *gasps!*

01:10:38.380 --> 01:10:39.900
Mark: Oh!
Amy: [text on-screen]

01:10:41.420 --> 01:10:43.980
Ryan: *gasping and coughing*

01:10:44.280 --> 01:10:45.120
Ryan: [text on-screen]

01:10:45.960 --> 01:10:47.760
Amy: [text on-screen]

01:10:48.980 --> 01:10:50.980
Ryan: [text on-screen]

01:10:55.460 --> 01:10:57.460
Amy: [text on-screen]

01:11:01.400 --> 01:11:03.400
Ryan:[text on-screen]

01:11:06.460 --> 01:11:08.460
Amy: [text on-screen]

01:11:09.560 --> 01:11:11.560
Ryan: [text on-screen]

01:11:15.940 --> 01:11:17.820
Amy: [text on-screen]

01:11:19.180 --> 01:11:21.180
Ryan: [text on-screen]

01:11:23.320 --> 01:11:25.320
Amy: [text on-screen]

01:11:28.180 --> 01:11:30.180
Ryan: [text on-screen]

01:11:33.280 --> 01:11:35.320
Amy: [text on-screen]

01:11:48.320 --> 01:11:51.500
Mark: That was about the most direct symbolism that's been in this game.

01:11:51.900 --> 01:11:53.060
Do I go in this again?

01:11:54.120 --> 01:11:56.380
Whoop- Noo, that's not what I...

01:11:56.700 --> 01:11:58.280
w-was doing...

01:11:58.400 --> 01:11:59.240
Well...

01:11:59.660 --> 01:12:03.340
Alright, then, I m-I missed out on some things.  Can I go back- I can't even go back.

01:12:03.660 --> 01:12:04.580
Can I go back?

01:12:04.820 --> 01:12:05.940
Ohhh, no...

01:12:05.940 --> 01:12:07.020
Sorry about that, guys.

01:12:07.020 --> 01:12:09.480
Mark: I really thought I was going for the life preserver.
Amy: [reads letter on-screen]

01:12:39.520 --> 01:12:40.060
Mark: Hm...

01:12:41.560 --> 01:12:43.620
Ahh, looks like I can't get back, either.

01:12:43.780 --> 01:12:45.000
Oh, maybe?

01:12:45.100 --> 01:12:46.980
Okay, good.  Sorry about that.

01:12:47.300 --> 01:12:50.320
I was just...very worried that I wasn't gonna be able to go over here.

01:12:50.740 --> 01:12:54.580
Now, what I'm gonna do here, is I'm only gonna get the note that is, I believe...

01:12:55.600 --> 01:12:58.040
related to the story, which is this one...

01:13:01.080 --> 01:13:03.080
Amy: [reads letter on-screen]

01:13:13.280 --> 01:13:14.360
Mark: Hmmm...

01:13:14.540 --> 01:13:16.260
Now, let me try this red one here.

01:13:20.420 --> 01:13:22.420
Woman: [reads letter on-screen]

01:15:16.640 --> 01:15:21.440
Mark: That was a fascinating departure from...everything that has been here so far.

01:15:21.900 --> 01:15:24.900
Like...there's a lot of stories out there.

01:15:25.680 --> 01:15:26.560
That's the thing.

01:15:26.960 --> 01:15:31.100
Tha-i-that's the thing that, like, it's another perspective thing. I-i-it's just another, like...

01:15:31.560 --> 01:15:36.820
generalization of what life is, in all of it's entirety.  There's so many different ways...

01:15:36.820 --> 01:15:38.840
Amy: [reads letter on-screen]

01:16:27.900 --> 01:16:29.000
Mark: Hmm...

01:16:31.500 --> 01:16:34.240
See, I'm... I'm wondering...

01:16:35.100 --> 01:16:40.460
I'm wondering if... 'Cause, like I said, there's multiple ways to face something...

01:16:41.060 --> 01:16:41.940
And...

01:16:42.940 --> 01:16:46.940
Like, I don't know if...the way she's going about it is...

01:16:47.360 --> 01:16:53.280
a good way, for it?  Always clinging onto hope, while also realizing the...the-the...

01:16:53.540 --> 01:16:58.980
the impossibility of the s- like, the-the challenge that she faces, or...you know...

01:16:59.500 --> 01:17:01.500
Amy: [reads letter on-screen]

01:18:02.920 --> 01:18:08.320
Mark: Yeah, becau- i-i-it's an interesting perspective, to see it from, like, an outsider.

01:18:08.440 --> 01:18:11.800
Looking at what she's experiencing, and...

01:18:12.840 --> 01:18:14.320
She is so sure...

01:18:14.460 --> 01:18:19.820
that this is the right action, and who am I to say that it's not?  Like I said, everyone deals with it in their own way.

01:18:19.980 --> 01:18:23.560
But also, at the same time, clinging...so hard to hope...

01:18:23.900 --> 01:18:29.440
can make you blind to everything else, and also the people around you, and...

01:18:29.940 --> 01:18:36.660
I'm not here to say one's wrong, or the other.  Like, I-I definitely want to emphasize that idea, that...

01:18:37.680 --> 01:18:38.500
Who knows?

01:18:39.320 --> 01:18:41.640
But at the same time...like...

01:18:42.440 --> 01:18:47.860
She's so sure, of her faith, a-and, and what she's feeling in there, while at the same time...

01:18:48.540 --> 01:18:50.240
The father, here, is drowning.

01:18:50.360 --> 01:18:53.460
And...maybe he needs help, you know?

01:18:53.980 --> 01:19:00.420
Maybe he needs help, an-and...and...her constant assurances, at the same time...

01:19:01.120 --> 01:19:02.240
Not helping him...

01:19:07.740 --> 01:19:08.740
Whoa, whoa!

01:19:08.900 --> 01:19:10.900
Whoa, am I...I'm not pointed in the right direction.

01:19:11.540 --> 01:19:12.460
Here we go.

01:19:12.960 --> 01:19:13.860
That's correct.

01:19:14.040 --> 01:19:14.860
Yeah...

01:19:15.680 --> 01:19:17.840
But, best not to let yourself drown.

01:19:19.880 --> 01:19:20.520
Oh...

01:19:21.440 --> 01:19:22.160
Okay...

01:19:24.540 --> 01:19:25.320
Yeah...

01:19:27.640 --> 01:19:31.720
Y'know, I s-I said I wasn't gonna talk about it, but I-I think it's probably just best that I do.

01:19:32.520 --> 01:19:35.400
It seems like...he's stuck.

01:19:39.360 --> 01:19:40.140
Come on...

01:19:40.480 --> 01:19:41.260
Come on.

01:19:41.860 --> 01:19:44.020
Come on... Ah, you're almost there.

01:19:45.520 --> 01:19:48.300
No... It's getting dark now.

01:19:51.140 --> 01:19:51.860
Yeah...

01:19:52.500 --> 01:19:56.520
I mean... I made it out- I probably made it out to seem like it was some...

01:19:57.220 --> 01:20:01.200
considerably dark story, and it was bad, but no.

01:20:01.960 --> 01:20:07.560
The story of when I first found out about my dad having cancer, i-i-it...

01:20:07.940 --> 01:20:11.720
Really, there's not a lot to it.  I-it's more of a perspective thing of...

01:20:11.900 --> 01:20:15.780
what I was talking about, like... No two people respond to it the same way.

01:20:16.080 --> 01:20:20.740
But, at the same time, mine was probably very typical.  Because, like he- they-

01:20:22.020 --> 01:20:24.360
My dad and my stepmom, they sat me down...

01:20:25.880 --> 01:20:26.900
at a table...

01:20:27.380 --> 01:20:33.840
And...i-they had gotten me lunch- or, dinner, from... I dunno, I believe Wendy's.

01:20:34.100 --> 01:20:38.600
And, I was just sitting there eating, and then they sat me down to have a very serious conversation, and...

01:20:39.900 --> 01:20:43.180
Like, what it was was just... I, uh...

01:20:46.020 --> 01:20:51.200
I... They told me the news, and at first...like, it didn't even register.

01:20:52.260 --> 01:20:56.920
You know, it didn't.  It was like, "oh, okay."  It- They might as well have told me the weather.

01:20:56.920 --> 01:20:58.500
You know, it was one of those things...

01:20:58.720 --> 01:20:59.620
And...

01:21:00.880 --> 01:21:04.360
I remember just sitting there, and it wasn't even like a conscious thing...

01:21:04.660 --> 01:21:07.280
It wasn't even like, uh...I processed it.

01:21:08.140 --> 01:21:09.980
It wasn't even like I calculated it.

01:21:10.040 --> 01:21:12.060
It wasn't like I thought about it at all.

01:21:12.060 --> 01:21:14.680
Like, what they said to me...went in.

01:21:14.740 --> 01:21:16.380
I went, "Okay."

01:21:18.180 --> 01:21:20.860
And then, I sat there for a few minutes.

01:21:21.340 --> 01:21:26.060
And then, all of a sudden, I didn't- I wasn't thinking, I wasn't feeling anything.  All of a sudden...

01:21:27.140 --> 01:21:28.900
Like, the full weight of it just hit me.

01:21:28.900 --> 01:21:32.860
It wasn't something that I actually comprehended, it was just the fact that...

01:21:34.620 --> 01:21:38.260
Like, the weight of what that meant hit me, and I just started crying.

01:21:38.920 --> 01:21:43.540
Like...harder than I've ever cried, just suddenly.  I couldn't stop, and it was...

01:21:43.560 --> 01:21:45.720
It was so weird, because...

01:21:46.000 --> 01:21:48.040
Just, the news.  And I, like, this is just...

01:21:48.580 --> 01:21:52.720
Like... I'm just saying this because, you know, I wanted to get this out in the open.

01:21:52.720 --> 01:21:54.960
There's nothing special to this story.  It's...

01:21:54.960 --> 01:21:58.000
It's a story that a lot of people have heard before, and obviously it doesn't...

01:21:58.200 --> 01:22:01.500
Like, I'm not going through as much pain as my dad was, probably.

01:22:02.020 --> 01:22:03.140
Or, definitely.

01:22:03.140 --> 01:22:04.860
A-it's just...

01:22:07.640 --> 01:22:08.480
I don't know...

01:22:09.360 --> 01:22:10.500
It's a perspective thing.

01:22:10.500 --> 01:22:13.500
And I know what this wants me to do, I was just pausing there so I could...

01:22:14.060 --> 01:22:15.360
tell that story, and...

01:22:16.420 --> 01:22:17.300
I don't know...

01:22:18.480 --> 01:22:19.260
Yeah...

01:22:21.300 --> 01:22:23.380
For some reason, it wanted him to swim downwards...

01:22:26.000 --> 01:22:27.020
*sighs*

01:22:27.980 --> 01:22:32.780
'Cause, this is what I meant when I said I wanted to take the appropriate time playing this game,

01:22:32.780 --> 01:22:34.420
because I knew it was gonna take me...

01:22:35.200 --> 01:22:38.480
back to a lot of things, and to a lot of places, and a lot of journeys.

01:22:38.480 --> 01:22:40.100
[Ryan reads text on-screen]

01:22:42.520 --> 01:22:43.220
Mark: Hm...

01:23:16.660 --> 01:23:18.780
Well, better get up, then.

01:23:22.380 --> 01:23:23.200
Hm...

01:23:31.700 --> 01:23:33.700
[Ryan]

01:23:39.020 --> 01:23:39.920
Mark: Well, I don't know...

01:23:47.360 --> 01:23:49.880
Hm... These are a lot of jumps to make.

01:23:50.120 --> 01:23:52.240
[Joel starts crying continuously in the background]

01:24:13.000 --> 01:24:14.000
Mark: Oh...

01:24:16.280 --> 01:24:17.320
*sighs* Oh.

01:24:19.040 --> 01:24:19.940
Alright, then.

01:24:21.500 --> 01:24:23.920
[buzzing sounds as Mark tries to hit the buttons]

01:24:27.460 --> 01:24:29.560
I guess there's no playing the game again.

01:24:30.800 --> 01:24:31.660
Hm...

01:24:34.100 --> 01:24:35.040
Okay.

01:24:37.520 --> 01:24:39.520
*sighs*

01:24:59.940 --> 01:25:00.900
[Joel stops crying and giggles briefly]

01:25:11.880 --> 01:25:14.260
[Joel starts screaming continuously]

01:25:20.040 --> 01:25:21.120
Mark: Oh, no...

01:25:26.240 --> 01:25:27.220
Ohh...

01:25:28.280 --> 01:25:30.280
[Ryan]

01:25:35.980 --> 01:25:36.780
Mark: Hm...

01:25:39.620 --> 01:25:40.480
Did I do it?

01:25:42.380 --> 01:25:44.640
Oh.  Food.  That was quick, wow.

01:25:47.880 --> 01:25:49.180
Back to the vinyl.

01:25:54.900 --> 01:25:56.900
[Ryan]

01:26:16.600 --> 01:26:18.600
[Joel finally stops screaming, and Ryan laughs slightly]

01:26:38.220 --> 01:26:40.540
[Joel's screaming starts again]

01:26:56.120 --> 01:26:56.860
Mark: Hm...

01:26:58.960 --> 01:27:00.380
Aww...

01:27:02.100 --> 01:27:03.380
*sighs*

01:27:03.380 --> 01:27:05.200
[Joel's screaming is drowned out by the sound of the rain]

01:27:05.200 --> 01:27:07.200
Mark: I mean-
[Ryan]

01:27:49.740 --> 01:27:50.740
Mark: Oh, man...

01:27:51.120 --> 01:27:54.640
'Cause, that's...that's another thing about the battle with cancer, like...

01:27:55.040 --> 01:27:57.160
That is...another thing, there...

01:27:57.160 --> 01:27:58.420
[Joel's screaming continues]

01:27:58.420 --> 01:28:03.380
Mark: It's not just one day, it's not an event, it's not the start or the end of it.  There's...

01:28:04.100 --> 01:28:14.000
weeks, months, and years involved with it.  There's an entire timeline of...just...living with this weight.

01:28:14.000 --> 01:28:16.000
[Ryan]

01:28:34.600 --> 01:28:36.600
[Ryan continues shushing]

01:29:16.920 --> 01:29:18.920
[Joel's screaming turning into coughing]

01:29:50.240 --> 01:29:52.240
[Joel's screaming stops]

01:30:05.620 --> 01:30:07.620
[Music stops]

01:30:13.100 --> 01:30:15.780
Mark: I mean, yeah, that's the thing, it's... It's...

01:30:17.800 --> 01:30:21.200
*sighs* It's...it's years...

01:30:22.320 --> 01:30:24.800
Years of struggle, sometimes.

01:30:24.800 --> 01:30:26.800
[Ryan]

01:31:35.540 --> 01:31:36.360
Mark: Hm...

01:31:46.020 --> 01:31:48.160
*sighs* Yeah...

01:31:48.720 --> 01:31:50.500
[voices fading in]
Amy: Look, look, oh!  We're in-

01:31:50.500 --> 01:31:56.240
Family: [together] Nevada!  We're in Nevada!  We're in Nevada!

01:31:56.240 --> 01:32:01.500
We're in California!!  Whooo!  *applause, horn honking*

01:32:02.120 --> 01:32:08.860
Ryan: *laughs*
Caleb: So, now that we're in California, how much longer to San Francisco?

01:32:08.860 --> 01:32:12.680
Ryan: About three and a half hours, bud.
Caleb: Awww...

01:32:12.680 --> 01:32:19.060
Amy: Well... It's 10 AM now, so that means you guys can grab one more item from your road trip bags.

01:32:19.160 --> 01:32:21.560
Isaac: And it's my turn to be the king!

01:32:24.620 --> 01:32:29.360
Mark: I'm assuming they went to California to try to pursue another form of treatment, which is, you know...

01:32:29.620 --> 01:32:34.880
When you're told...that, you know, there's nothing else to be done, you know...

01:32:35.260 --> 01:32:37.580
Parents aren't gonna take that.
[Family starts singing in background]

01:32:37.580 --> 01:32:41.960
Like, you always... You always pursue something like that.  Because, when-

01:32:41.960 --> 01:32:43.960
[Ryan]

01:32:52.320 --> 01:32:53.080
Mark: Hm...

01:32:53.360 --> 01:32:58.000
Family: [still singing] 🎵They are weak, but He is strong🎵

01:32:58.740 --> 01:33:03.100
🎵Yes, Jesus loves Joel🎵

01:33:03.100 --> 01:33:07.300
🎵Yes, Jesus loves Joel🎵

01:33:07.300 --> 01:33:12.940
🎵Yes, Jesus loves Jo~el, la la la la la🎵

01:33:12.940 --> 01:33:17.000
Ryan: 🎵He loves Joel so much! Oh, he loves Joel!🎵

01:33:17.220 --> 01:33:22.000
Family: *finishes the song*

01:33:22.260 --> 01:33:22.980
Mark: Hm...

01:33:30.200 --> 01:33:32.200
[Ryan]

01:34:44.740 --> 01:34:45.680
Mark: Hm...

01:34:47.800 --> 01:34:48.760
*sighs*

01:34:53.120 --> 01:34:59.420
I'll probab- I'll wrap up my thoughts at the end of this, I just... I have a funny feeling it's getting closer to...

01:35:00.540 --> 01:35:04.100
maybe not the end of the game, but the end of this section in the game, I'm not sure.

01:35:05.700 --> 01:35:09.000
I mean, I go- I have a lot of thoughts on this, because of my personal experience through it,

01:35:09.000 --> 01:35:10.580
but that doesn't mean that I know...

01:35:11.540 --> 01:35:12.580
the right answers.

01:35:14.760 --> 01:35:15.520
Anyway...

01:35:17.100 --> 01:35:19.100
[Amy]

01:35:33.600 --> 01:35:35.600
[Ryan]

01:35:35.920 --> 01:35:37.920
[Amy]

01:35:38.340 --> 01:35:40.340
[Ryan]

01:35:58.520 --> 01:35:59.220
Mark: Huh...

01:36:00.240 --> 01:36:00.940
Yeah...

01:36:03.420 --> 01:36:06.020
Yeah, I wish I had more thoughts, right now.

01:36:06.460 --> 01:36:09.040
I really do.  I wish I had more thoughts about this.

01:36:09.820 --> 01:36:15.140
I-I wish, like, I had more personal experience to relate about this...section, here.

01:36:16.120 --> 01:36:17.060
Because...

01:36:17.860 --> 01:36:18.640
Whoa.

01:36:21.620 --> 01:36:23.180
That is intimidating.

01:36:23.220 --> 01:36:24.080
Hmm...

01:36:24.920 --> 01:36:28.780
Man, this is... This is intimidating, here.

01:36:28.780 --> 01:36:33.440
TV Voice: Alright, kids, you know what time it is!
Kids: Yaaaay!
[Fun music playing]

01:36:33.440 --> 01:36:34.460
Mark: What time is it?

01:36:35.200 --> 01:36:36.700
I don't know what time it is.

01:36:38.980 --> 01:36:42.760
Is it symbolic that the...sword and shield are broken now?

01:36:43.740 --> 01:36:44.820
Man, I don't know...

01:36:45.180 --> 01:36:48.220
I mean, there's a lot of symbolism in this game, and if obviously this is a...

01:36:48.220 --> 01:36:53.360
This is a religious portion of the game, but like, it's important to remember that this specific portion...

01:36:53.560 --> 01:36:57.560
is still a part of their experience, and the reason I was saying, like...

01:36:57.620 --> 01:37:02.380
Who am I to judge what people believe in?  The reason I say that is because...

01:37:02.380 --> 01:37:09.420
From one person's perspective to another...whatever brings someone hope, in a situation like this...

01:37:09.920 --> 01:37:14.320
Who am I to remove that hope?  Or, who is anyone to remove that hope?

01:37:14.320 --> 01:37:17.720
From anyone who has been affected by this?

01:37:18.700 --> 01:37:24.140
And I've said this over and over, the entire time that I've played this: There is no right way to handle something.

01:37:24.540 --> 01:37:31.640
And this level may be called The Temple of God, which is very...very...very interesting.

01:37:32.480 --> 01:37:35.960
But at the same time...  Some people, you know...

01:37:36.660 --> 01:37:41.060
It doesn't matter what you believe in.  Everyone...can still get cancer.

01:37:41.580 --> 01:37:46.920
And everyone needs to remember to be kind to one another in these experiences, because...

01:37:47.800 --> 01:37:50.800
At the end of it all, you know...like...

01:37:51.140 --> 01:37:55.980
Death is the great unifier in what we do, and what I remember from...

01:37:56.120 --> 01:37:59.180
my experiences with it...you know, are...

01:38:02.040 --> 01:38:04.900
You know, they're one thing amongst many.

01:38:05.460 --> 01:38:10.700
Anyway... I-I'm rambling again, I have n- I didn't really know what I was talking about there, so...

01:38:10.860 --> 01:38:13.080
I won't make an assumption that I do.

01:38:13.080 --> 01:38:15.960
[voices speaking in the background multiply as candles are lit]

01:38:21.340 --> 01:38:22.040
Mark: Hm...

01:38:24.760 --> 01:38:25.500
Oh.

01:38:27.160 --> 01:38:29.480
[musical chord starts playing, mixed with the voices]

01:38:50.280 --> 01:38:52.620
[all the noise fades out]

01:38:52.620 --> 01:38:54.620
[church music starts playing]

01:38:56.440 --> 01:38:57.160
Mark: Oh...

01:38:57.160 --> 01:38:59.160
[the voices start up in the background again]

01:38:59.480 --> 01:39:00.460
Mark: Man...

01:39:12.060 --> 01:39:13.020
I-I...

01:39:13.420 --> 01:39:16.820
I honestly don't wanna... I don't know what to make of this.

01:39:21.440 --> 01:39:22.180
Man...

01:39:39.680 --> 01:39:40.900
Whoa.  Okay.

01:39:41.120 --> 01:39:42.280
I don't know what I did.

01:39:42.660 --> 01:39:43.440
Alright.

01:39:44.440 --> 01:39:45.560
Something's happening.

01:39:45.960 --> 01:39:46.780
Okay...

01:39:49.420 --> 01:39:54.460
