01:45:41.420 --> 01:45:42.100
*chuckles*

01:45:43.240 --> 01:45:43.920
Yeah...

01:45:52.620 --> 01:45:54.620
[Joel laughs and claps]

01:46:22.180 --> 01:46:23.320
Mark: I'm guessing...

01:46:23.920 --> 01:46:27.020
I'm guessing that's the end, because that's representative of...

01:46:27.480 --> 01:46:30.660
I'm guessing, Joel in the afterlife.

01:46:31.240 --> 01:46:32.580
And that's the end of the game.

01:46:33.580 --> 01:46:36.660
That was a... That was a really interesting experience.

01:46:37.780 --> 01:46:39.060
"Joel Evan Green"

01:46:41.040 --> 01:46:41.940
I mean...

01:46:42.400 --> 01:46:45.880
It's...it's so fascinating.

01:47:00.180 --> 01:47:04.560
*tearful* That was weird.  Just seeing his picture, like made it really real for a second there.

01:47:31.600 --> 01:47:34.800
*crying*

01:47:36.120 --> 01:47:37.180
That was, um...

01:47:40.620 --> 01:47:43.300
It's just a moving experience, 'cause...

01:47:43.600 --> 01:47:44.980
I-I don't know...

01:47:45.860 --> 01:47:47.300
*choked* I don't know these people.

01:47:49.400 --> 01:47:50.220
*breathes*

01:47:52.940 --> 01:47:54.580
But, I can, like...you know...

01:47:55.120 --> 01:47:56.540
I can see...

01:47:58.500 --> 01:48:00.080
like, what they've gone through.

01:48:03.000 --> 01:48:09.580
And...and that's the thing, you know... My dad...my dad died from cancer, and...

01:48:10.100 --> 01:48:12.920
It's...it's not the cancer...

01:48:14.320 --> 01:48:16.320
that, you know, that I think about.

01:48:16.320 --> 01:48:21.380
You know, it's not the cancer itself that I...you know, look back on.

01:48:21.380 --> 01:48:24.920
'Cause I don't want that to be the memories that I have of my dad.

01:48:25.480 --> 01:48:29.200
You know, and I- it's not even something, anymore that, like...

01:48:29.400 --> 01:48:34.620
I don't- it's not like it keeps me awake at night, you know, I'm fine...uh, now.

01:48:34.620 --> 01:48:41.220
And I was fine, you know...not too...too much longer after my dad passed away.

01:48:41.480 --> 01:48:43.360
An-and that's the thing, it's...

01:48:43.980 --> 01:48:48.580
The hardest times...are the struggle during...

01:48:48.580 --> 01:48:52.060
And...the pain of seeing, during-- Hi.

01:48:52.360 --> 01:48:55.480
For the first time this whole gameplay, Chica came up to say Hi.

01:48:56.740 --> 01:48:59.880
Chica normally records with me, she's just a very...quiet pup.

01:49:00.860 --> 01:49:03.800
And, it's just- you know, it's-it's not...

01:49:05.060 --> 01:49:10.600
I-it's not... It's not 'after' that gets me sad, it's not...'before' that gets me sad.

01:49:10.600 --> 01:49:14.520
I don't look back at all the memories that I had with my dad, and I don't get sad.

01:49:15.180 --> 01:49:20.340
You know, I may get teary-eyed, because I look back fondly on the times that we had together, but it's...

01:49:20.920 --> 01:49:25.060
You know, it's the struggle that really...really tears me up.  Knowing that...

01:49:25.100 --> 01:49:25.980
You know...

01:49:27.380 --> 01:49:31.060
It's that sense of helplessness that really, really...

01:49:32.460 --> 01:49:33.420
affects people.

01:49:34.300 --> 01:49:39.980
It's the sense of not being able to do anything, when all you want in the world is to be able to do something.

01:49:41.720 --> 01:49:43.220
You know...and that's... *choking up*

01:49:43.960 --> 01:49:53.300
In the time of greatest need, when you wish that, in all the world, the only thing that you could possibly want...

01:49:53.760 --> 01:49:55.480
is to be able to help that person.

01:49:55.480 --> 01:49:57.800
Like, you would give anything- *chokes up*

01:50:03.620 --> 01:50:10.260
And, like I said before, you know, I don't know what it's like to be a father, and I don't know what it's like to be a...

01:50:10.540 --> 01:50:16.000
You know...to see a child go through those things, but I'd like to think that...

01:50:16.400 --> 01:50:17.240
you know...

01:50:17.520 --> 01:50:20.520
I'd at least feel that same feeling of...

01:50:21.640 --> 01:50:25.040
the desire to do absolutely anything to help.

01:50:26.600 --> 01:50:28.020
You know, you would give...

01:50:30.380 --> 01:50:31.500
You'd give anything.

01:50:34.140 --> 01:50:38.580
*sniffs* You'd give absolutely anything to be able to help.

01:50:39.740 --> 01:50:41.980
And, it's the feeling that you can't...

01:50:42.560 --> 01:50:44.020
There's nothing you can do.

01:50:48.460 --> 01:50:50.660
And those are the times that get you down.

01:50:50.660 --> 01:50:53.840
Those are the times that I look back and I actually get sad for.

01:50:55.840 --> 01:50:58.620
And seeing, like, the changes that go through...

01:51:00.560 --> 01:51:05.920
you know, the family, and my dad himself.  You know, seeing...him...

01:51:06.460 --> 01:51:07.840
you know, change...

01:51:08.220 --> 01:51:13.540
That's hard to deal with.  That is brutal to deal with, and this game painted it in a very...

01:51:16.500 --> 01:51:21.460
I can't say "good" like, 'cause it's not a good experience.  It's not a good thing, but...

01:51:21.860 --> 01:51:23.360
This was a game...

01:51:24.280 --> 01:51:25.760
that, like, I...

01:51:26.420 --> 01:51:29.120
I-I'm really happy that I played it.

01:51:30.180 --> 01:51:34.740
*sigh* So- I feel- You know, it's bizarre, I feel oddly good.

01:51:34.740 --> 01:51:39.940
I feel...I feel really good, I thought... I thought, when I came out of this experience, I was gonna be like...

01:51:40.460 --> 01:51:43.900
so unbelievably sad, but I feel good.

01:51:44.200 --> 01:51:45.240
Like, I remember...

01:51:45.240 --> 01:51:50.380
Like, when I went through that journey, I had so many memories of the times that I was with my dad.

01:51:50.500 --> 01:51:58.040
And even through the struggle, even through the hard times, even through the worst of it... I remember my dad.

01:51:59.400 --> 01:52:05.700
And he's such a huge inspiration to me, and he's such a huge reason why I'm the person I am today.

01:52:05.700 --> 01:52:12.200
And he's such a huge reason...why I push myself to try to be better every day.

01:52:12.640 --> 01:52:18.820
And it's amazing to see, and I feel good.  It's really bizarre, I feel really good.

01:52:20.660 --> 01:52:24.240
Because, I think the end of that game, the-the thing that it was trying to come across-

01:52:24.240 --> 01:52:26.520
And this whole game was like an experience of feelings.

01:52:26.700 --> 01:52:31.080
It was like a storybook of emotions of this...this family, and what they went through and...

01:52:31.140 --> 01:52:35.240
And at the end, it was...it was supposed to be a feeling of peace.

01:52:35.600 --> 01:52:39.760
Like, not necessarily hope, but a feeling of...of peace.

01:52:41.880 --> 01:52:43.360
And that's...you know...

01:52:43.780 --> 01:52:47.620
Take that for- whatever way you want, whatever you will, but...

01:52:48.220 --> 01:52:51.320
I don't know... Like, that...that connected with me.

01:52:52.040 --> 01:52:54.100
Like, I felt that peace, because...

01:52:54.600 --> 01:52:56.600
I'm at peace with...you know...

01:52:57.400 --> 01:53:03.700
my dad...passing, and I'm at peace with who I am, and I'm at peace with the fact that he didn't get to see...

01:53:03.740 --> 01:53:05.320
who I am now.

01:53:06.920 --> 01:53:08.040
And that's okay.

01:53:10.080 --> 01:53:12.080
'Cause, I've been very fortunate.

01:53:12.600 --> 01:53:14.340
And a lot of people haven't.

01:53:15.880 --> 01:53:22.620
And...thankfully, I haven't had to experience...cancer, personally.  I haven't had to go through it, and...

01:53:23.100 --> 01:53:25.620
And- I've had a tumor, but it wasn't cancerous.

01:53:25.620 --> 01:53:28.920
Like, I don't want anyone to get the wrong idea, that I've been through chemotherapy,

01:53:28.920 --> 01:53:31.000
or I've been through anything like that.  I haven't.

01:53:31.380 --> 01:53:32.220
And, um...

01:53:33.160 --> 01:53:33.840
Y'know...

01:53:34.600 --> 01:53:37.040
It's just... I don't know.

01:53:37.500 --> 01:53:38.560
I don't feel sad.

01:53:38.960 --> 01:53:40.040
I really don't.

01:53:40.680 --> 01:53:46.680
And...I-I just want to say, thank you everybody, so much, for asking me to play this game, and asking me to...

01:53:47.020 --> 01:53:51.240
go through this, and I really hope that I gave it the attention that it deserved because

01:53:51.240 --> 01:53:56.000
I wanted to make sure that I went into this...with, like, eyes wide open, and...

01:53:56.140 --> 01:54:00.120
taking in absolutely everything from this, and I feel like...

01:54:00.680 --> 01:54:04.000
this was an experience that need...needed to be made.

01:54:04.200 --> 01:54:06.200
Like, this game needed to be made.

01:54:06.800 --> 01:54:10.840
Not necessarily for any one specific person, but just in general.  It needed...

01:54:11.400 --> 01:54:13.220
You know, it needs to exist.

01:54:13.460 --> 01:54:17.500
If...only to tell this family's story.

01:54:18.580 --> 01:54:24.960
So, anyway... I-I'll... That's about all I have to wrap up with this.  I could tell more stories about...

01:54:25.160 --> 01:54:27.760
my dad, but I'll save that for another day.

01:54:27.940 --> 01:54:33.460
I-I've said a lot...throughout this video, that I didn't think I was gonna talk about, and...

01:54:34.560 --> 01:54:37.520
You know... Just, thank you everybody so much for listening.

01:54:37.520 --> 01:54:43.400
And, uh, also...you know, just closing stuff.  Uh, I did mention at the beginning of this video.  Um...

01:54:43.760 --> 01:54:46.720
You know, there is information about the Crisis Text Line, which is...

01:54:47.060 --> 01:54:52.360
the charity that we're-we're doing, a lot of the people in Revelmode are doing, uh, this next week,

01:54:52.360 --> 01:54:53.660
upcoming for a while.

01:54:53.900 --> 01:54:59.180
And, you know, that's...that's another important element.  Because, cancer is one thing, but there's...

01:54:59.640 --> 01:55:02.400
There's so much more... Being human is hard. *chuckles slightly*

01:55:02.440 --> 01:55:05.560
Being human is really, really hard.  And...

01:55:06.360 --> 01:55:09.680
There's so many things that...need to be helped, and...

01:55:10.340 --> 01:55:12.420
There's no time to be petty, and...

01:55:12.880 --> 01:55:14.400
There's no time to be...

01:55:15.460 --> 01:55:16.420
You know...

01:55:17.940 --> 01:55:20.140
hold grudges against people.

01:55:21.140 --> 01:55:24.840
I'm not talking about anything specifically, I'm just talking in general, like..

01:55:25.120 --> 01:55:28.040
There-there's no time for it, because...

01:55:29.820 --> 01:55:31.900
You don't know how much time you have.

01:55:32.520 --> 01:55:33.620
You really don't.

01:55:34.380 --> 01:55:37.500
And you have to make the best of it while you can.

01:55:38.960 --> 01:55:44.840
So, anyway, that's...that's literally all I have.  Check the description for more... uh... important information, and...

01:55:44.840 --> 01:55:47.160
Please support the developers of this game, and...

01:55:47.400 --> 01:55:50.780
And give warm regards to the family...

01:55:51.080 --> 01:55:54.020
who was a part of this, I believe it's the Green family, so...

01:55:54.500 --> 01:55:56.260
Anyway... I'll leave with that.

01:55:56.740 --> 01:55:58.640
Thank you everybody so much for watching.

01:55:58.640 --> 01:56:02.460
Thank you for sticking with me through this...way-too-long video.

01:56:02.660 --> 01:56:05.860
And, thank you for everyone pushing me to play it, because...

01:56:05.860 --> 01:56:10.760
I didn't want to play it, but I may have been putting it off a little bit because I didn't know if I wanted to go through it

01:56:10.760 --> 01:56:14.960
